# Build context filter for the api and worker images (both build from the repo
# root). Without this file `COPY . .` in worker/Dockerfile ships the whole
# repo - .git, web/node_modules, the measurement archive - and any change to
# any of it invalidates the layer and rebuilds from there.

# .env holds the OpenAI key. It is gitignored, but gitignore does not apply to
# a build context: before this file existed, `COPY . .` baked it into the
# worker image. Compose passes it in via env_file at runtime; it must never be
# a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.github

# The web image builds from ./web with its own context, so nothing here needs
# the frontend - least of all node_modules.
web/

# Python build noise
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Corpora: read by eval and replay on the host, never inside a container.
# data/dictionaries/ is NOT excluded - masking loads the name list at runtime.
data/*.jsonl

# Measurement archive (gitignored, but the build context does not know that)
olcum-arsivi/

docs/
*.md
